5. CARDS

Cards should use:

background:
#151116

border:
1px solid #332B33

border-radius:
16px

padding:
20px to 24px

shadow:
very subtle

Example:

.card {
background: #151116;
border: 1px solid #332B33;
border-radius: 16px;
padding: 22px;
transition:
transform 160ms ease,
border-color 160ms ease,
background 160ms ease;
}

.card:hover {
transform: translateY(-2px);
border-color: #4A3D49;
}

6. BUTTONS

Buttons should be compact and tactile.

Primary button:

- Accent background
- Dark text
- Rounded pill
- Slight hover movement

Secondary button:

- Transparent / panel background
- Thin border
- Light text

Example:

.primary-button {
background: #D97832;
color: #160F0B;
border: 0;
border-radius: 999px;
padding: 11px 17px;
font-family: "Space Grotesk";
font-weight: 700;
cursor: pointer;
transition: 160ms ease;
}

.primary-button:hover {
background: #EA8B3F;
transform: translateY(-1px);
}

.secondary-button {
background: #151116;
color: #F1E9DE;
border: 1px solid #332B33;
border-radius: 999px;
}

7. PILLS

Use pill-shaped elements for:

- Versions
- Status
- Statistics
- Tags
- Categories
- Small controls

Example:

.pill {
display: inline-flex;
align-items: center;
gap: 7px;

padding: 7px 11px;

border-radius: 999px;

background: #1B161C;
border: 1px solid #332B33;

color: #B8AFB5;

font-family: "IBM Plex Mono";
font-size: 12px;

}

